{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3540","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3540","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3540\",\"parent_revision\":\"33a6e52bf08bfcff9245c06210c08fb22ccb62568e7eecafc238f0ef794a362b\",\"root_revision\":\"33a6e52bf08bfcff9245c06210c08fb22ccb62568e7eecafc238f0ef794a362b\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-13\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nRoughly 20 files in the tree reference `TeamCreate`, and several recommend using it. The call no longer exists: `plugins/agent-orchestration/skills/delegate/references/harness-notes/claude-code.md` records that as of Claude Code v2.1.178, naming a teammate on an `Agent` call while `CLAUDE_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_AGENT_TEAMS` is enabled spawns it directly, with no separate setup step, and that the `swarm-*` skills documenting the old flow were retired in favour of `parallel-work`.\\n\\nConfirmed positive recommendations include `plugins/plugin-creator/SKILL.md` at lines 48 and 815. This is plugin content, not research corpus, so it was outside the scope of the PRs that surfaced it.\\n\\nAn agent following any of these writes a delegation against a primitive that is gone. The failure is silent at authoring time \u2014 the instruction reads as valid and only fails when executed.\\n\\nThis is the same drift class the research corpus repair addressed today: PR #3391 renamed `.claude/rules/` to `rules/` and PR #3422 removed the swarm skills, between them breaking 99 citations across 83 files that were all correct when written. Those were repaired in PR #3531. The `TeamCreate` references are the same shape in a different corpus, and nothing detects them.\\n\\nTwo distinct questions the grooming should separate: what each of the ~20 references should say now, and whether anything should detect this class of drift in plugin content going forward. Related open items on the detection half: #3534 (entry review cannot express path drift) and #3535 (claims are checked after the irreversible filing step, not before).\\n\\n**User-provided context**: the count was established during review of PR #3531 as 20 files, correcting an earlier figure of 19 that appeared in a banner across 36 research entries. That banner text has since been corrected in the merged PR. Duplicate detection matched five unrelated items on generic keywords (#3037, #3054, #3223, #3262, #3266); none concern this subject and the item was filed with force.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 round-two review of PR #3531 (merged as 2a733bebd)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-13\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"7dbe92702ff1462a9c3f1953c0c5a9d95b694e00905b6d5d0e1dc4f3b79ad0b3\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABUeTJyA\"}"}